      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to understand the pattern of the series. The series alternates between adding and subtracting terms. The terms are given by \\(1 + 3k\\) where \\(k\\) starts from 1 and increases by 1 each time.\n\nLet's break it down step-by-step:\n\n1. Identify the number of terms in the series.\n2. Calculate the sum using the pattern.\n\nThe series is \\(1, -4, 7, -10, 13, \\ldots, 55\\). Notice that each term alternates between positive and negative. To find the number of terms, we need to identify the general term of the sequence. \n\nThe general term \\(a_k\\) can be described by the formula:\n\\[ a_k = 3k - 2 \\]\nwhere \\(k\\) is the position of the term in the sequence.\n\nTo find the number of terms \\(n\\), we need to determine when the \\(n\\)-th term is equal to 55.\n\n\\[ 55 = 3n - 2 \\]\n\\[ 57 = 3n \\]\n\\[ n = 19 \\]\n\nSo, there are 19 terms in the series. Since the series alternates, half of them will be positive and the other half will be negative. Thus, there will be 9 positive terms and 9 negative terms.\n\nThe sum S will be the sum of the 9 positive terms minus the sum of the 9 negative terms.\n\nLet's calculate the sum using the pattern:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Sum} = (1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - 16 + 19 - 22 + 25 - 28 + 31 - 34 + 37 - 40 + 43 - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55)\n\\]\n\nWe can write a Python code to calculate this sum accurately.\n\nLet's implement this in Python:\n```python\n# Define the function to calculate the sum of alternating series\ndef alternating_series_sum():\n    total_sum = 0\n    num_terms = 0\n    \n    for k in range(1, 100):\n        term = 3 * k - 2\n        total_sum += term\n        num_terms += 1\n        \n        if term == 53:  # Could be adjusted based on the problem statement, ensuring it's the last term\n            break\n    \n    # Calculate the number of positive and negative terms\n    pos_terms = num_terms // 2\n    neg_terms = num_terms - pos_terms\n    \n    # Sum the positive and negative terms\n    positive_terms_sum = sum(term for term in range(1, pos_terms + 1, 2))\n    negative_terms_sum = sum(term for term in range(2, neg_terms + 1, 2))\n    \n    # The final sum\n    return total_sum - (positive_terms_sum * 2 + negative_terms_sum)\n\n# Calculate the sum\nresult = alternating_series_sum()\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n236\n```\nThe value of the expression \\(1 - 4 + 7 - 10 + 13 - \\cdots - 46 + 49 - 52 + 55\\) is \\(\\boxed{236}\\).",
